# Provenance

Four public sources, each used under its own terms, and one simulator. Nothing here identifies a traveler: the on time files have no passenger, the registry is kept to the aircraft, and the check log stores airports, hours and buffers.

{{ statement() }}

## The Bureau of Transportation Statistics: Reporting Carrier On-Time Performance

Public domain as a work of the U.S. government. Monthly files from `https://transtats.bts.gov/PREZIP/On_Time_Reporting_Carrier_On_Time_Performance_1987_present_<year>_<month>.zip`, downloaded one at a time with retries by `deploy/fetch-data.ps1` on a machine that could reach the host. {{ v('data.months') }} files of {{ v('data.months_expected') }} expected from {{ v('data.first_month') }} to {{ v('data.last_month') }}; missing months: {{ v('data.gaps') }}. {% if raw('data.next_month_unpublished') == 1 %}The fetch on {{ v('data.fetched_on') }} also asked for {{ v('data.next_month') }} and BTS had not published it yet, which is why the window stops at {{ v('data.last_month') }}.{% else %}The fetch did not record asking for {{ v('data.next_month') }}, so the window's end is the last month on disk, not a checked latest month.{% endif %} {{ v('data.layout_matches') }} files matched the field layout their own readme describes. {{ v('data.rows') }} rows in all. {{ v('data.tails_restored') }} rows ({{ v('data.tails_restored_share') }}, from {{ v('data.tails_restored_carriers') }}) reported the aircraft's registration without its leading N; the N is restored when the result is a valid registration, and the value as reported stays beside it as `tail_reported`.

